From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] arm: meson: caches on from U-Boot's start

BL31 enters U-Boot (BL33) with the MMU and both caches off, and U-Boot
turns them on only after relocation: until then every instruction fetch,
load and store goes to DRAM. On the ODROID-GO Ultra (S922X) that was
~1.7 s between U-Boot's start and the board info, more than the whole
rest of U-Boot without the boot delay.

arch_cpu_init() now turns both caches on, with page tables of their own
16 MiB below the early stack, DRAM nothing uses before relocation. The
relocation flushes what it copied (relocate_code() does it when the data
cache is on); enable_caches() after it turns the data cache off, writes
it back, and on again with the tables reserved at the top of RAM, as
before. From start to board info: 1.69 s -> 0.18 s.

A U-Boot chainloaded by one that left its MMU on (no "dcache off" before
"go") would build on the first one's page tables, in RAM it is about to
overwrite: the data cache goes off first.

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-meson/board-common.c b/arch/arm/mach-meson/board-common.c
index c34b81e5e78..a34a0a0460a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-meson/board-common.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-meson/board-common.c
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@
 #include <cpu_func.h>
 #include <fastboot.h>
 #include <init.h>
+#include <system-constants.h>
+#include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <net.h>
 #include <asm/arch/boot.h>
 #include <env.h>
@@ -31,6 +33,40 @@ __weak int board_init(void)
 }
 
 #ifndef CONFIG_SPL_BUILD
+/*
+ * BL31 enters U-Boot (BL33) with the MMU and both caches off, and U-Boot
+ * turns the caches on only after relocation: until then every instruction
+ * and every load and store goes to DRAM, ~1.7 s on the S922X between
+ * U-Boot's start and the board info. Turn them on at once, with page
+ * tables of their own below the early stack (DRAM that nothing uses
+ * before relocation). The relocation flushes what it copied; after it,
+ * enable_caches() moves to the tables reserved at the top of RAM.
+ */
+#define EARLY_TLB_ADDR	(SYS_INIT_SP_ADDR - SZ_16M)
+
+int arch_cpu_init(void)
+{
+	/*
+	 * Chainloaded by a U-Boot that left its MMU on (no "dcache off"):
+	 * its page tables are in the RAM this one relocates to. Off first.
+	 */
+	dcache_disable();
+	gd->arch.tlb_addr = EARLY_TLB_ADDR;
+	gd->arch.tlb_size = PGTABLE_SIZE;
+	icache_enable();
+	dcache_enable();
+	return 0;
+}
+
+void enable_caches(void)
+{
+	/* off, written back, and on again with the reserved tables */
+	dcache_disable();
+	gd->arch.tlb_fillptr = 0;
+	icache_enable();
+	dcache_enable();
+}
+
 int dram_init(void)
 {
 	const fdt64_t *val;
